llvm-4.0.0 backport patch: a protected thread-local stays general-dynamic in a shared object (PS4)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION for a thread-local variable a -fPIC
(non-PIE) unit defines at protected visibility. Upstream r273921
(8121becac311, 2016-06-27, "Teach shouldAssumeDSOLocal about tls"),
first released in 3.9.0, made TargetMachine::getTLSModel take IsLocal
from shouldAssumeDSOLocal, which is true for any non-default visibility,
so a protected definition is local-dynamic (`leaq x@TLSLD`, `x@DTPOFF`).
LLVM 3.8 gave local-dynamic only to a local or hidden symbol. The base
has general-dynamic at all 21,974 thread-local sites and local-dynamic
at none (D23, round 124A). This patch restores 3.8's condition inside
the shared-library branch only. With it the game module's thread-local
stand-ins are protected like every other (D50, D51): FUN_00d6a930
compiles to the base's bytes and no matched game row changes (round
145B).

--- a/lib/Target/TargetMachine.cpp	2026-11-11 03:57:04.439595384 +0000
+++ b/lib/Target/TargetMachine.cpp	2026-11-11 03:57:04.448461707 +0000
@@ -173,7 +173,10 @@
 
   TLSModel::Model Model;
   if (IsSharedLibrary) {
-    if (IsLocal)
+    // PS4: the shared-library rule of LLVM 3.8 (before r273921): only a
+    // local or hidden symbol is local-dynamic; a protected one stays
+    // general-dynamic.
+    if (GV->hasLocalLinkage() || GV->hasHiddenVisibility())
       Model = TLSModel::LocalDynamic;
     else
       Model = TLSModel::GeneralDynamic;
